# Activity 3: Real-Time Flood Monitoring Infographic

## Description
This activity required designing an educational infographic titled **"Real Time Flood Monitoring"**[cite: 4]. It walks readers through four numbered sections explaining what flooding is in the Philippines, why communities lack timely localized alerts, how water-level sensor systems provide real-time SMS/mobile warnings, and how to interpret Safe, Warning, and Critical alert levels[cite: 4].

## What Have I Learned?
- **Key Concepts & Skills:** I learned how to break down technical disaster-preparedness information into a logical numbered flow (`Monitor → Detect → Warn → Prepare → Respond`) supported by icons, color-coded warning indicators, and academic references[cite: 4].
- **Challenge & Solution:** Fitting detailed explanations, community needs, warning signs, and citations onto a single page without overcrowding was challenging; I solved this by grouping related points into distinct content blocks with clear headings and bullet lists[cite: 4].
- **Future Application & Improvement:** Infographics are especially valuable in community health nursing for educating residents on environmental hazards and emergency preparedness, and I could improve this piece by increasing the font size of the references section for easier reading.
